    "result_text": "BUILD SUCCESS \u2014 all tests pass.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the soft-duplicate (\"possible duplicate\") detection for owner creation. When a new owner isn't a hard duplicate but shares an existing owner's `lastName` + `postcode` with a *different* telephone, it's still created and flagged.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added two read-only fields to the `Owner` schema: `possibleDuplicate` (boolean) and `possibleDuplicateOf` (int32, present only when true). These regenerate into `OwnerDto`, and MapStruct auto-maps them by name.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 Added persisted `possibleDuplicate` / `possibleDuplicateOf` fields (columns `possible_duplicate`, `possible_duplicate_of`) with getters/setters, so the values survive to the `GET /api/owners/{id}` read the test uses.\n\n3. **Schema/seed SQL** \u2014 Added the two columns to all four `schema.sql` variants (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres) and padded the positional owner inserts in `db/hsqldb/data.sql` (the other data files use explicit column lists, so were unaffected).\n\n4. **`FlagOwnerPossibleDuplicate.java`** (new pipeline function) \u2014 Runs on the built owner before save (so it can't match itself). It sets `possibleDuplicate` false by default, then scans existing owners for one with the same postcode, same last name (case-insensitive), and a *different* telephone; on a match it sets `possibleDuplicate` true and `possibleDuplicateOf` to the earliest-created match's id. Hard duplicates are already rejected upstream by `CheckOwnerIdentityUnique`, so this only flags genuine soft matches.\n\n5. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 Wired the new step into the transactional pipeline between `bulkSignup` and `save`.\n\nThe new acceptance test `coreFlagsPossibleDuplicate` passes, and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
